The --env flag is a preset over the individual ppx flags: `development`
equals --dev (marker classes), `production` equals --minify (minified CSS,
no markers). The classes and rules are the same in both modes; only the
markers and the sheet's line breaks differ.

  $ refmt --parse re --print ml input.re > input.ml

With --env development, classNames carry a cx-<binding> marker and no
[@@@css.config] is emitted (absence means development).

  $ ../../standalone.exe --env development --impl input.ml -o dev.ml
  $ refmt --parse ml --print re dev.ml
  [@css ".css-1992jrt{display:flex;padding:12px;}"];
  [@css ".css-1y4lziy{color:red;}"];
  [@css.classes
    [
      ("css-1992jrt", 0, "Input.layout", "input.ml", 1, 22, 1, 52),
      ("css-1y4lziy", 1, "Input.button", "input.ml", 2, 22, 2, 34),
    ]
  ];
  [@css.bindings
    [("Input.layout", "css-1992jrt"), ("Input.button", "css-1y4lziy")]
  ];
  let layout = CSS.make("cx-layout css-1992jrt", []);
  let button = CSS.make("cx-button css-1y4lziy", []);
  let _ = (layout, button);
  $ styled-ppx.generate dev.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  .css-1992jrt{display:flex;padding:12px;}
  .css-1y4lziy{color:red;}

With --env production, the same classes appear without markers, and the PPX
declares the environment in the wire protocol so styled-ppx.generate
minifies its output without any flag.

  $ ../../standalone.exe --env production --impl input.ml -o prod.ml
  $ refmt --parse ml --print re prod.ml
  [@css.config [("env", "production")]];
  [@css ".css-1992jrt{display:flex;padding:12px;}"];
  [@css ".css-1y4lziy{color:red;}"];
  [@css.classes
    [
      ("css-1992jrt", 0, "Input.layout", "input.ml", 1, 22, 1, 52),
      ("css-1y4lziy", 1, "Input.button", "input.ml", 2, 22, 2, 34),
    ]
  ];
  [@css.bindings
    [("Input.layout", "css-1992jrt"), ("Input.button", "css-1y4lziy")]
  ];
  let layout = CSS.make("css-1992jrt", []);
  let button = CSS.make("css-1y4lziy", []);
  let _ = (layout, button);
  $ styled-ppx.generate prod.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  .css-1992jrt{display:flex;padding:12px;}.css-1y4lziy{color:red;}

An unknown environment is rejected by the driver.

  $ ../../standalone.exe --env staging --impl input.ml -o out.ml 2>&1 | grep -o "wrong argument.*"
  wrong argument 'staging'; option '--env' expects one of: development production.
